mmit checks passed, and the dispute parser reads it as one FIX for F1.\n\nBecause the plan is at its cap, only a DISMISS lets the pass record be written, so this ruling now goes to the owner. The coordinator recipes say anything other than an accepted DISMISS at the cap means closing the lane partial.\n\n**Why the finding holds, from the code at the range:**\n- **The record check uses the peel's attestor.** P5 recognises the machinery's close only through `mechanical_close_attestation`, and that attestor deliberately refuses any changed path outside `docs/work/`.\n- **The real close relinks across the whole repo.** `close_adjudication` archives each row through `spec_move.move_spec`, which rewrites and stages inbound markdown links in every file. A relative link to the row's spec from a review, plan or log file therefore produces a genuine machinery close that the attestor refuses.\n- **The lane is left with no way to land.** Today such a close only loses its peel, so the gate asks for one more review. Under P5, an adopting close in that shape is refused at the merge slot and at the hook. The plan's stated recovery, \"a person re-closes it\", is a hand close that P5 itself refuses and P7 removes. Reverting the close removes the record, which is also refused, and `close_adjudication` won't run again once the row has left `active/`.\n- **It is reachable, though rare so far.** Reviewers in this repo do link specs by relative paths; the wave-5 review files link adjudication specs this way. Adjudication lanes that mint successors are reviewed while the row is still active, so the link lands before the close. None of the 18 mechanical closes in history touched anything outside `docs/work/`.\n- **It is a Done-when gap.** The Done-when says the commit check \"passes the close's own commit\", and P5 would refuse a supported close. That makes it convergence-class, so it can't be ruled SUCCESSOR.\n\n**How this differs from my WI-925 dismissal:** that miss failed into a hold an